# What `docker compose build` is allowed to send to the daemon.
#
# Without this file the ENTIRE working directory is uploaded as the build context on
# every build - .git, .venv, the 133 MB UCI dataset, pgdata, and .env. None of it is
# copied into the image (infra/Dockerfile takes only pyproject.toml, README.md, src/
# and data/), but the context is transferred and cached regardless, and a secret that
# travels to the daemon is a secret in one more place than it needs to be.

# --- version control and agent scratch ---
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.claude

# --- secrets: must never enter a build context ---
.env
*.key
secrets/
infra/mosquitto/passwd

# --- local environments and caches ---
.venv
venv
__pycache__
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.coverage
htmlcov
*.egg-info

# --- runtime state and generated output ---
anchor/
out/
pgdata/
models/
artifacts/
data/household_power_consumption.txt
data/ground_truth.csv

# --- not part of the runtime image ---
tests/
docs/
web/
.github/
*.md
!README.md
